            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "In optics, the thin lens formula is ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "\\frac{1}{f}=\\frac{1}{u}+\\frac{1}{v}",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ".",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p40-q7-instruction",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Show that ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "f=\\frac{uv}{u+v}",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", then write this as a compound fraction.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$f=\\frac{uv}{u+v}=\\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{u}+\\frac{1}{v}}$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{f}&=\\frac{u+v}{uv}\\\\f&=\\frac{uv}{u+v}\\end{align*}$$\nTaking the reciprocal of the original formula gives the compound fraction:\n$$f=\\frac{1}{\\frac{1}{u}+\\frac{1}{v}}.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 48
